===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|wange}}, from {{inh|de|goh|wanga}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|wang}}, {{cog|en|wang}}. See the latter for more.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈvaŋə/}}
* {{rhymes|de|aŋə|s=2}}
* {{audio|de|De-Wange.ogg}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|f|dim=^chen,^lein,^elein}}

# {{lb|de|chiefly|formal|or|literary}} [[cheek]] (on the face)
#: {{syn|de|Backe}}

====Usage notes====
* A more normal word for “cheek” is {{m|de|Backe}}. In literary style, however, ''Wange'' is common and even preferred to some degree.

